abstract: >-
  Python code, research data and interactive visualisations produced by
  Remoboko: Religion, Morality and Boko in West Africa, a Leibniz Junior
  Research Group (2018-2024) at Leibniz-Zentrum Moderner Orient (ZMO), Berlin,
  funded through the Leibniz Competition. The project studied religiosity and
  its effects on secular education (boko, in Hausa), examining the coexistence, competition and conflict between
  secularism, Salafism and Pentecostalism on four West African campuses:
  Université Abdou Moumouni (Niamey, Niger), University of Ibadan (Nigeria),
  Université de Lomé (Togo) and Université d'Abomey-Calavi (Benin). The
  repository contains the maps, timelines, charts and word clouds created for
  the monograph "Religious Activism on Campuses in Togo and Benin" and for the
  project's final report.
